# Feature workflow & docs

## Where specs live

- Feature requirements: **`docs/features/*.md`** (user stories: *As a / I want to / So that* + acceptance criteria).
- **Live delivery tracker:** **`docs/features/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md`** (✅ implemented, 🟡 partial/mock/UI-only, ❌ missing).
- **Test coverage matrix:** **`docs/features/TEST_COVERAGE.md`** — maps user stories to unit / integration / E2E tests (keep in sync when tests change).

## After code changes

When you implement, extend, or remove a feature, **update `IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md`** in the same PR/conversation so status matches reality.

When you add, move, or remove automated tests, **update `TEST_COVERAGE.md`** for the affected stories.

## Conflicts

If a story file under `docs/features/` disagrees with **`IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md`**, treat the **status doc** as the shipped-truth for "what exists now," and either fix the story file in a follow-up or note the drift in the status doc.

## New work

For non-trivial features: add or extend a spec under **`docs/features/`** and add/update rows in **`IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md`** before or alongside implementation (avoid landing code with no doc anchor).
